<title>UK: SOCCER-ENGLISH LEAGUE AND CUP RESULTS.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-ENGLISH LEAGUE AND CUP RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results of English league and cup</p>
<p>soccer matches on Tuesday:</p>
<p>F.A. Cup third round</p>
<p> Barnsley	  2  Oldham		    0</p>
<p>(Barnsley away to Queens Park Rangers in</p>
<p>in fourth round)</p>
<p> Brentford	 v  Manchester City	 postponed</p>
<p>(Eventual winners at home to Watford or Oxford)</p>
<p> Carlisle	  1  Tranmere		  0</p>
<p>(Tranmere at home to Sheffield Wednesday)</p>
<p> Chesterfield    2  Bristol City	    0</p>
<p>(Chesterfield away to Luton or Bolton)</p>
<p> Crewe	     1  Wimbledon		 1</p>
<p>(Eventual winners away to Manchester United)</p>
<p> Crystal Palace  2  Leeds		     2</p>
<p>(Eventual winners away to Arsenal or Sunderland)</p>
<p> Gillingham	0  Derby		     0</p>
<p>(Abandoned after 66 minutes - frost. Eventual winners</p>
<p>at home to Notts County or Aston Villa)</p>
<p> Luton	     v  Bolton		    postponed</p>
<p>(Eventual winners at home to Chesterfield)</p>
<p> Notts County    0  Aston Villa	     0</p>
<p>(Eventual winners away to Gillingham or Derby)</p>
<p> Watford	   v  Oxford		    postponed</p>
<p>(Eventual winners away to Brentford or Manchester City)</p>
<p>Third round replay</p>
<p> Huddersfield    1  Queens Park Rangers   2</p>
<p>(QPR at home to Barnsley)</p>
<p>Division three</p>
<p> Scarborough     1  Cambridge		 0</p>
<p> Swansea	   3  Barnet		    0</p>
<p> Chester	   0  Rochdale		  0</p>
<p> Colchester	2  Fulham		    1</p>
</text>
